AF]plus their pyo3 bindings.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Python status model and presentation[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]py-status[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-status[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Phase py-status: Python status model and presentation' section: add [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Status.CLAIMED, the SQLite migration, the shared bead status [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]presentation module, and every read-side CLI surface.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Runner claim lifecycle[/bold #D7AFFF]                                        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]py-claim-runtime[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-claims, py-status[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Phase py-claim-runtime: Runner claim lifecycle' section: claim the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]canonical bead store when a bead-carrying agent starts waiting, promote [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]on launch, and release on shutdown.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Stale claim reconciler and doctor check[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]chop-reconciler[dim] · [dim][/dim]after py-claim-runtime[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Phase chop-reconciler: Stale claim reconciler and doctor check' [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]section: add the bead_claim_checks chop that releases claims held by [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]dead pre-launch agents and a doctor advisory for unowned claims.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]ACE and clan summary visuals[/bold #D7AFFF]                                  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]tui-visuals[dim] · [dim][/dim]after py-status[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Phase tui-visuals: ACE and clan summary visuals' section